course: dictionary
lesson: 9512
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number. To pick the right one, read the words around the word: this is its context. «Mia keeps her stickers.» Children usually keep stickers as pictures to stick on things, so this sticker is the small picture.
explain: The phrase «a sheet of stickers» is another clue. A sheet of stickers is a page of small pictures you can peel off and stick on your books or lunch box. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes you need the place as a clue. A price sticker is found in a shop, not in a playground. It is a small label that shows how much something costs. The same word can mean a picture or a label, and the setting tells you which.
fact: A «sticker» is a small picture or label with glue on the back that you can stick on things.
fact: A «price sticker» is a small label in a shop that shows how much something costs.
fact: Stickers are a thing you can count: one sticker, two stickers, a sheet of stickers.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, the context tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence. If it makes sense, you have probably got it right.
exercise: «Mia keeps her stickers.» What is a sticker in this sentence? | A loud noise in a shop | A sheet of paper for writing on | A tiny bag for lunch | *A small picture or label with glue on the back
exercise: What is a price sticker? | In a book about trains | *A small label in a shop that shows how much something costs | A sign on the top of a hill | Inside a bicycle wheel
exercise: How do you know that sticker is a noun that can be counted? | It never has a plural | *You can say one sticker or many stickers | You can only use it with the word very | It is always a name for a person
test: What does a price sticker show? | The name of the shop owner | *How much something costs | Where to park the car | How old a shop is
test: Which meaning fits «a sheet of stickers»? | A type of shoe | A large glass window | A road sign with arrows | *Small pictures with glue on the back, sold on paper
exam: A teacher gives you a sticker for good work. Which meaning of sticker fits best? | *A small picture or label with glue on the back | A loud sound made by a machine | A tiny bag for carrying lunch | A small label in a shop that shows the price
